  "summary": "古赋以寡宿比喻武曲的孤克倾向，提及女命、火星和婚姻不利；作者区分旺宫会吉与不见吉、多煞的情形，认为前者可表现为负责、谋定而动、顾及他人，后者较易寡合。寡宿与将星在此是武曲性质的称谓，不另指同名小星。",
  "summary_en": "Classical texts describe Wu Qu metaphorically as a solitary star and discuss female natives, Huo Xing, and marital difficulties. The author contrasts strong-palace placement with many auspicious stars against no auspicious support or many harmful stars: responsibility, planning and consideration versus interpersonal isolation. Gua Su and Jiang Xing here describe Wu Qu, not separate minor stars. Classical adverse conditions mention Kong Jie and Si Sha; the Huo Xing passage claims early separation or middle-age widowhood, not an established case or timing chart. Another quoted favorable condition requires strong Life Palace or Body Palace placement, auspicious support from three directions and no harmful clash.",
